# AudioWRT-owned packages that genuinely compile upstream source and therefore
# need an OpenWrt development dependency staging path.
#
# Packages NOT listed here are still compiled when they contain AudioWRT source
# code, but they stay on the NO_DEPS=1 package boundary. Runtime-only OpenWrt
# dependencies must never turn into source-build roots.
#
# Wi-Fi ownership:
# - audiowrt-wpad compiles one multicall hostapd+wpa_supplicant binary from the
#   exact OpenWrt hostap source, but stays on the NO_DEPS=1 boundary.
#   scripts/build.sh stages only its required development interfaces from
#   exact-release sources/APKs so hostapd-common/ubus/ucode never become
#   recursive source-build roots.
#
# Bluetooth ownership:
# - audiowrt-bluez builds both audiowrt-bluez and audiowrt-bluez-libs.
# - audiowrt-btctl is AudioWRT-owned C code and is package-only.
# - audiowrt-sbc is derived upstream source but has no external build dependency
#   and remains package-only.
# - bluez-alsa and audiowrt-bluez are the only Bluetooth upstream source roots.

librespot
audiowrt-bluez
bluez-alsa
